{
  "dom_id": "step-q71580",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{8}{x-2y+3z}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{8}{x-2y+3z} & =c \\\\ 8 & =c(x-2y+3z) \\\\ cx-2cy+3cz-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y,z)$ can't be zero. Therefore, we get a family of planes:\n\n$$\ncx-2cy+3cz-8=0,\\,c\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
